From 7dbf2fe33a2e62564bfc854721a0f5a83a651cd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:10:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Keymap: a key can be bound to Do nothing

A head unit's key handler often delivers presses that were never meant
for the projection. On cars whose factory system keeps the steering
wheel (an Audi MMI, for one), the wheel's OK still reaches this app and
Android Auto selects whatever has focus. The keymap could not help: its
"Remove binding" leaves the key unbound, and an unbound key goes on to
Android Auto as itself.

- InputAction.Ignore, stored as "ignore", offered in the keymap's action
  picker as "Do nothing", right below "Remove binding". A key bound to it
  goes nowhere on press or release, and the press is logged.
- Keys only: the gestures' picker does not offer it, since a gesture's
  "Disabled" already does nothing; a gesture that somehow holds it does
  nothing as well.
- An older build reads "ignore" as unbound, so a downgrade sends the key
  again rather than doing anything unexpected.

The keymap help says what Do nothing is for, in every locale.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WfvDdsw9pz4kqjTjiNxyCC
